@BDY_PART_DESC_0(ARG)
#FUNCTIONS
SELECTCASE ARG
	CASE 0
		RETURNF "The entire body. Effectively this is for hediffs (Health Differences) that affect the whole body as a whole and cannot be directly damaged."
	CASE 1
		RETURNF "The most important part of a human, the head includes the ears, brain, forehead, cheeks, chin, eyes, nose, and mouth. Loss of the head means instant death."
	CASE 2
		RETURNF "Aesthetic part that gives humans their beauty."
	CASE 3
		RETURNF ""
	CASE 4
		RETURNF "Parts that give characters their vision, and the loss of sight will make them blind. The lack of sight can significantly affect accuracy."
	CASE 5, 6
		RETURNF "Ears allow humans to hear noises. Without an ear, it will be difficult to hear things, and having no ears will make someone deaf."
	CASE 7
		RETURNF ""
	CASE 8
		RETURNF "A mouth conceals the tongue and throat, and also allows humans to talk and eat."
	CASE 9
		RETURNF "A tongue is how people can taste things, as well as a crucial part for talking. Having no tongue will make them unable to speak"
	CASE 10
		RETURNF ""
	CASE 11
		RETURNF "A very important part as it allows blood to circulate between the head and the rest of the body. Necks are also very vulnerable to bleeding, and bleed rapidly, which can result in death within minutes"
	CASE 12
		RETURNF "What your head conceals, and an essential part for life. This is the main factor for Consciousness and an injured brain directly affects it. Death happens when this part hits 0%, not -100%"
	CASE 20 TO 23, 30 TO 33
		RETURNF "Appendages for holding things. Both must be working properly to hold two-handed weapons. Having no arms or hands will result in you being unable to hold anything. A critical hit to the arm will result in an artery bleed, significantly more critical compared to a normal bleed due to the increased hemorrhage. "
	CASE 40
		RETURNF "Center of mass, also known as the torso. Contains many vital organs for your body to function. Loss of the thorax means instant death."
	CASE 41 TO 44
		RETURNF "Lactates milk and gives a lot of sex appeal. Affects Fertility"
	CASE 45, 46
		RETURNF "Allows you to breathe. Losing both lungs means instant death. You can still live with just one."
	CASE 47
		RETURNF "Pumps blood from your heart to other parts of your body. Death happens when this part hits 0%, not -100%"
	CASE 51
		RETURNF ""
	CASE 52
		RETURNF "Midsection of the torso. Doesn't really do a lot."
	CASE 53
		RETURNF "Stores food. Losing this means total bowel incontinence"
	CASE 54
		RETURNF "What used to be a port for an umbilical cord"
	CASE 55
		RETURNF "Your back. Mainly has your spine. Don't have your spine break, or you cannot move at all"
	CASE 56, 57
		RETURNF "Appendages at the back that allow for conventional flight. Youjutsu-based flight is still possible even without wings."
	CASE 58
		RETURNF ""
	CASE 60
		RETURNF "Lower section that connects your legs. Don't have your hips break, or you cannot move at all"
	CASE 61
		RETURNF "Area where your genitals sit."
	CASE 62 TO 64
		RETURNF "Female reproductive system and hosts a fetus. Keep this intact if you want to have a baby!"
	CASE 65
		RETURNF "Fun buns that allow you to sit."
	CASE 66
		RETURNF "Keeps waste in the body until its time to go. Losing this means total bowel incontinence"
	CASE 67
		RETURNF "Stores solid waste. Losing this means total bowel incontinence"
	CASE 68 TO 71
		RETURNF "Male reproductive system. Stores sperm and perfectly fits inside a female vagina for reproduction. Keep this intact if you want to have a baby!"
	CASE 72
		RETURNF "Tube where urine passes through. Losing this means total urinary incontinence"
	CASE 73
		RETURNF "Animallike extension to your body. Moves and wags with you."
	CASE 74
		RETURNF "Stores urine. Losing it means you cannot hold your pee, making you drip pee right into your underwear."
	CASE 75, 76
		RETURNF "Filters waste products into urine. Losing both kidneys means instant death. You can still live with just one."
	CASE 77
		RETURNF "Helps keep your blood pure. Hitting 0% or lower means instant death."
		;	CASE 80
		;		RETURNF "L leg"
	CASE 81 TO 83, 91 TO 93
		RETURNF "Appendages for moving. Injured legs make your move slower. Having no legs or bound legs makes it impossible to normally move. A critical hit to the leg will result in an artery bleed, significantly more critical compared to a normal bleed due to the increased hemorrhage."
ENDSELECT
